{"id": "EUVD-2026-102294", "enisaUuid": "9db71e09-b9da-3eba-93fa-8bceba58a1ee", "description": "GNU LibreDWG through 0.14.8612 contains a global out-of-bounds read vulnerability in the AcDs decoder acds_private() that allows attackers to read beyond a static table via an unchecked schema property type index. Attackers can supply a crafted R2004 or R2010+ DWG file with a large 'schdat' property type value to crash dwgread, dwg2dxf, or any application using LibreDWG.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:09:43", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libredwg-acds-schema-prop-type-oob-read", "https://github.com/LibreDWG/libredwg/blob/d9468ae948b8f07a08efa756c19f8916052358c0/src/acds.spec#L250-L260", "https://github.com/LibreDWG/libredwg", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/gnu-libredwg-through-0.14.8612-out-of-bounds-read-in-acds-private-acds-decoder"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jgcr-6xrx-cmqc", "CVE-2026-111167"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "bc70129b-1439-3f4a-9c94-2ce1ccccd098", "product": {"name": "libredwg", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.14.8612"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "85f325de-0329-30f4-8f7a-426fc99004e9", "vendor": {"name": "GNU"}}], "isExploited": false}